  "addressing": "P001-P030 are one-based physical printed 6/8 regions on one page. Five grand-staff systems at pypdfium2 scale 2.5 (6+7+5+6+6). P001 is a one-eighth opening pickup. P002-P008 are complete 6/8 bars. P009 is a five-eighth first-strain terminal (capacity 5/2) closed by the combined repeat at x=813. P010 is a one-eighth second-strain pickup closed by the staff-spanning barline at x=894. P011-P029 are complete 6/8 bars. P030 is a five-eighth terminal (capacity 5/2) before a thin-plus-thick close that also carries backward-repeat dots. Combined repeat after P009 / forward start before P010. Backward close after P030. Pickup-plus-terminal pairs: 1/2+5/2=3 (P001+P009) and 1/2+5/2=3 (P010+P030). No volta.",
  "source_frame_evidence": "Inspected one page render at pypdfium2 scale 2.5 (1570x1905) plus five grand-staff children from staff-line detection with inter-system midpoints. Printed tempo Vivace dotted-quarter=100, 6/8 on both staves, one flat. RH opens G clef line 2; LH opens F clef line 4. LH changes to G in P008 after bass A3, C4, and F4 (last 3 notes A4, F4, G4 in treble) and returns to F on the last eighth of P012 (first governed event is the staccato C3 eighth in the second space, no ledger). Combined repeat at P009/P010; staff-spanning barline at x=894 splits the second-strain pickup P010 from full P011. Backward close after P030. System-start clefs are reprints. P030 ends with a cautionary G, backward-repeat dots, and a thin-plus-thick close. Five systems 6+7+5+6+6 = 30 printed regions. No musical ink on the page boundary.",
